| `TimezoneOffset` — minutes to add to UTC to get the clock the reader is
| looking at. +120 in Berlin in summer, -300 in New York, 0 in UTC.
|
| `Timestamp` cannot answer "what day is it here", and for anything a person
| reads that is the only day that counts: a task due today sits in
| yesterday's column for a third of the planet if the answer is UTC.
|
| The bounds are the real ones: no zone is further out than +14
| (Kiritimati) or -12.

emit TimezoneOffset to core get z
assert z._class = "TimezoneOffsetResult"
assert z.value ≥ 0 - 720
assert z.value ≤ 840

| It must agree with itself from one moment to the next — the offset is a
| property of where this is running, not of when it was asked.
emit TimezoneOffset to core get again
assert again.value = z.value

| And it composes with `Timestamp` the way a caller will use it: local
| seconds are UTC seconds plus the offset, which stays a whole second.
emit Timestamp to core get t
local = t.value + z.value * 60
assert local ≥ t.value - 43200
assert local ≤ t.value + 50400
